    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied when two operands can be compared by the comparator selected by <computeroutput>Op</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The comparison is the one made by the <computeroutput>apply()</computeroutput> function of the comparison tag: by value for the integers of different signedness (see <computeroutput>sign_mixed_integers</computeroutput>), otherwise with the operator of the language. A function pointer compared with an object pointer is also accepted (see <computeroutput>function_pointer_pair</computeroutput>). Used to reject the call of <computeroutput>eq()</computeroutput> and of the other comparators at the call site, with a short diagnostic; the operator check is the first alternative, so that the Clang diagnostic names the invalid operator and the two types first (GCC reports only that no alternative is satisfied).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Op</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The comparison. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type deduced for the left hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type deduced for the right hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
